Three rectangular bites are cut from a 16 cm by 10 cm rectangle (the bites are shown dashed):

- bite A: a 3 cm by 3 cm square from a corner;
- bite B: 2 cm wide and 4 cm deep, from the middle of the bottom edge;
- bite C: 3 cm tall and 2 cm deep, from the middle of the right edge.

Find the perimeter and the area of the shape that remains.

![A 16 cm by 10 cm rectangle with three rectangular bites removed: a square from the top-left corner, a deep narrow notch from the middle of the bottom edge, and a notch from the middle of the right edge.](asset:q31-fig1)
